  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency protection intervention in Sake, North Kivu, and Minova, South Kivu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through a community -based protection approach, the project places communities at the heart of the response. It supports the creation and revitalisation of community protection structures, the establishment of referral systems, and the provision of Cash for Protection to enable victims of abuse and violence to access essential protection services quickly. At the same time, essential infrastructure will be rehabilitated (water points, latrines, showers, solar streetlights), thereby helping to reduce protection risks, particularly violence during water collection &#x2013; a key moment when women and children are often at increased risk of gender -based violence (GBV). The initiative will also promote women&apos;s leadership, the inclusive participation of people with disabilities and young people, as well as the accountability of local authorities through training and advocacy grounded in community realities. Information and awareness -raising activities will raise awareness of the crisis in the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) and its needs, in order to maintain the attention of the public and decision -makers and to support the mobilisation of international resources. By combining protection with access to water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) services, this project aims to restore the security, dignity and resilience of populations affected by conflict in North and South Kivu.</narrative>
  </description>
